WEBVTT

00:02.990 --> 00:04.530
This target...

00:07.850 --> 00:10.040
It's a challenge from us.

00:10.040 --> 00:13.820
You should take
the game tomorrow, Bookmaker.

00:43.440 --> 00:45.110
GODS' GAME WE PLAY

00:46.480 --> 00:51.740
GODS' GAME WE PLAY

01:45.590 --> 01:49.010
PLAYER.09: BOOKMAKER

01:49.010 --> 01:50.070
Retry...

01:50.540 --> 01:51.510
Comeback...

01:52.230 --> 01:54.750
Nel? Hey, Nel?

01:54.750 --> 01:57.190
I can do this...
I'll do this...

01:59.820 --> 02:02.250
W-What are you doing, Pearl?!

02:02.250 --> 02:06.190
It's like your senses have flown
to another world, Nel.

02:06.190 --> 02:10.650
I'm sorry.
I made this situation more intense.

02:10.650 --> 02:14.360
No problem.
I was just thinking about something too.

02:14.360 --> 02:17.080
Are you thinking about Bookmaker?

02:17.860 --> 02:19.810
Well, something like that.

02:19.810 --> 02:23.290
Bookmaker is different from other gods.

02:23.650 --> 02:25.990
It's a game of 1 vs. 1 between
a human and a god.

02:27.380 --> 02:30.040
The bet is "one win" from
a member of the party.

02:30.530 --> 02:32.830
This time, my "one win" will be the chip.

02:33.340 --> 02:36.470
If you win, your defeat is reduced by one.

02:36.470 --> 02:38.480
But if I lose,

02:38.900 --> 02:42.100
you will lose one of your precious wins.

02:42.100 --> 02:43.310
I don't mind at all.

02:43.310 --> 02:44.700
Master Fay?!

02:44.700 --> 02:47.270
You're just ruining
the tenseness of this game!

02:47.270 --> 02:50.130
I knew I had no right to say this,

02:50.130 --> 02:53.740
but I think you should be more
proud of your achievements!

02:54.180 --> 02:55.530
Is that so?

02:55.990 --> 02:59.400
The average win rate
in the gods' game is 1%,

02:59.790 --> 03:01.950
one win is 10 times more
critical than one loss.

03:02.420 --> 03:04.720
However,
Master Fay has now won six games.

03:05.120 --> 03:07.560
Having an unprecedented 10 wins
is not a dream anymore.

03:08.050 --> 03:09.090
Well, yeah.

03:09.090 --> 03:12.710
But what I can say is that you don't
have to be overly concerned.

03:12.710 --> 03:13.860
What does that mean?

03:13.860 --> 03:14.920
We have chances to win.

03:14.920 --> 03:17.370
Woah, that's Fay for you!

03:17.370 --> 03:19.880
So you mean you have
a secret plan to win?

03:19.880 --> 03:20.930
No, I don't.

03:20.930 --> 03:25.520
T-Then, did you figure out which game
was best to challenge Bookmaker?

03:25.520 --> 03:26.880
No.

03:26.880 --> 03:29.650
Then, how do you know
we have a chance to win?

03:29.650 --> 03:32.110
Because the opponent is Bookmaker.

03:32.110 --> 03:32.840
Huh?

03:32.840 --> 03:34.460
What does that mean?

03:34.460 --> 03:38.510
I wish I could tell you,
but unfortunately, I'm not sure yet.

03:38.510 --> 03:41.830
I've never played
against Bookmaker before.

03:42.310 --> 03:46.500
Leshea, are you really don't want
my one win begone because Nel loses?

03:46.850 --> 03:48.000
She won't lose.

03:49.460 --> 03:51.170
We have a chance, right?

03:51.170 --> 03:52.130
Yep.

03:52.130 --> 03:53.910
Then we should take the challenge.

03:53.910 --> 03:56.590
Nel, I'm rooting for you.

03:56.590 --> 03:59.050
Y-Yes! Lady Leshea!

03:59.050 --> 04:02.350
You're not going to lose, are you?

04:02.350 --> 04:06.310
Huh? W-Well... Of course I'll do my best.

04:06.310 --> 04:07.590
Yeah, you must.

04:07.590 --> 04:12.750
After putting in all this expectation,
there's no way you're going to lose.

04:12.750 --> 04:14.730
Even at the World Games Tour,

04:14.730 --> 04:17.070
we bluntly refused you
and asked you to turn back,

04:17.070 --> 04:19.030
so you can't do something like that.

04:22.910 --> 04:24.540
Huh? What's wrong?

04:24.920 --> 04:26.370
She fainted!

04:26.370 --> 04:29.310
Lady Leshea was unintentionally
putting pressure on Nel!

04:29.310 --> 04:32.660
Nel! Get the hang of yourself!

04:37.580 --> 04:39.800
Welcome back, Lady Leoleshea.

04:39.800 --> 04:41.120
Good job, Fay.

04:41.530 --> 04:44.390
And welcome back too, Pearl.
You did a great job.

04:44.390 --> 04:46.310
T-Thank you very much.

04:46.310 --> 04:51.100
I have a feeling you've been a promised
apostle from the moment you joined here.

04:51.100 --> 04:53.310
You can be an apostle
to carry our branch!

04:53.310 --> 04:55.650
That's too sudden!

04:55.650 --> 04:58.180
Well, let's put that kind of joke aside.

04:58.590 --> 04:59.490
Nel.

04:59.490 --> 05:00.890
Y-Yes!

05:01.420 --> 05:04.280
I'm so sorry
for the trouble I've caused you.

05:04.280 --> 05:07.200
Um, here's a Mal-ra's maju as a souvenir!

05:07.200 --> 05:08.650
Wow.

05:08.650 --> 05:10.080
That's unusual.

05:10.730 --> 05:12.440
Well, to be honest,

05:12.440 --> 05:15.650
as the Chief Secretary,
I don't want to push you,

05:15.650 --> 05:18.590
but since you're going to do it,
do your best and make a comeback.

05:18.590 --> 05:21.010
T-Thank you very much!

05:21.010 --> 05:23.890
So, when do you want to
challenge Bookmaker?

05:23.890 --> 05:26.140
I'm fine anytime.

05:26.140 --> 05:28.870
Then, I guess the earliest you can go
is the day after tomorrow.

05:28.870 --> 05:32.690
Fay, just to make sure,
we have a chance to win, right?

05:32.690 --> 05:33.820
Yes.

05:35.610 --> 05:37.610
RUIN BRANCH - GIRL'S DORMITORY

05:37.610 --> 05:41.070
Let's begin this welcome party!

05:41.070 --> 05:44.530
Well, Nel, please make yourself at home
in this small room.

05:44.530 --> 05:46.490
Thank you.

05:46.490 --> 05:49.450
It's totally fine.
I mean, look.

05:49.950 --> 05:53.690
This bed is amazing!
It's absorbing me!

05:53.690 --> 05:55.920
It's so soft, I can't get up.

05:56.540 --> 05:57.920
Right?

05:57.920 --> 06:00.940
This is the "bed that once you
sleep on it, you can't get up"

06:00.940 --> 06:04.010
that I spent my salary last year to buy.

06:04.980 --> 06:06.100
Zzz...

06:06.440 --> 06:08.810
Wait, you already slept?!

06:08.810 --> 06:10.560
Thank you, Pearl.

06:10.560 --> 06:12.640
You gave me such a warm welcome.

06:13.020 --> 06:14.600
Please don't mind about it.

06:14.600 --> 06:18.540
You know, Fay and Lady Leshea
are my goals, or rather,

06:18.540 --> 06:21.650
for an ordinary person like me,
they are my aspirations.

06:21.650 --> 06:24.580
So I thought it would be nice
to have someone

06:24.580 --> 06:28.700
I could talk to and ask
to work together and get closer.

06:28.700 --> 06:31.370
Pearl! You're so kind!

06:34.810 --> 06:36.830
I know how you feel!

06:36.830 --> 06:39.380
We can't always be ordinary people.

06:39.380 --> 06:42.210
We must grow up
to be able to help them!

06:42.210 --> 06:45.050
Y-Yes, that's what I thought.

06:45.050 --> 06:46.970
But first,

06:46.970 --> 06:48.930
why don't we take a bath?

06:48.930 --> 06:49.900
A bath?!

06:49.900 --> 06:52.390
Oh, you can join us too, Lady—

06:52.850 --> 06:54.930
I just remembered something urgent.

06:54.930 --> 06:56.800
You two can take a bath without me.

07:03.850 --> 07:05.130
It seems Lady Leshea

07:05.130 --> 07:09.610
always has something urgent to do
when I ask her to take a bath.

07:15.830 --> 07:17.950
This bath is so much prettier
than my bathroom.

07:17.950 --> 07:19.790
It's so different from mine.

07:20.390 --> 07:22.500
How's the hot water?

07:22.500 --> 07:24.280
Ah, just right in the—

07:28.200 --> 07:30.600
H-How magnificent...

07:31.530 --> 07:34.660
I already thought they were big
when you were wearing clothes,

07:34.660 --> 07:36.770
but they were even bigger
when you were naked!

07:36.770 --> 07:40.860
Ah, my underwear
has become tight again recently.

07:40.860 --> 07:45.230
So maybe they look more big
when I take off my underwear.

07:45.230 --> 07:47.110
So you free them from the seal!

07:47.110 --> 07:48.740
What do you mean?!

07:49.210 --> 07:51.700
What do you mean,
"I'm an ordinary person"?!

07:51.700 --> 07:54.500
You have such an enviable thing!

07:54.900 --> 07:57.630
It's as if you have
watermelons in your chest!

07:57.630 --> 07:59.460
Do you think I play
some magic tricks?!

07:59.830 --> 08:01.960
They're so large
that you can't hide them.

08:02.290 --> 08:05.460
It is so large that it protrudes from
your back even if you turn your back.

08:05.820 --> 08:08.010
Despite their mass,

08:08.010 --> 08:10.750
they're wonderfully round
without collapsing at all.

08:10.750 --> 08:12.400
Smooth like a baby,

08:12.400 --> 08:15.760
the cleavage that naturally forms
without pushing it from either side

08:15.760 --> 08:18.210
is soft yet sensational!

08:18.210 --> 08:20.230
You don't have to explain it!

08:21.470 --> 08:22.730
So bouncy...

08:22.730 --> 08:24.690
Don't use onomatopoeic words either!

08:25.020 --> 08:27.580
If Pearl's is the summit of the gods,

08:27.580 --> 08:28.760
then mine is

08:28.760 --> 08:31.340
the great plain as far
as the eye can see.

08:31.340 --> 08:33.700
Is that supposed to be a poetic expression?!

08:36.000 --> 08:37.080
What a defeat...

08:37.080 --> 08:40.620
So, this is what Lady Leshea sensed
and then left this room...

08:41.130 --> 08:43.430
Um, Nel?

08:43.900 --> 08:45.540
Oh, that's right.

08:45.540 --> 08:48.840
You have your good points, don't you, Nel?

08:50.240 --> 08:52.300
Your charm...

08:52.680 --> 08:54.760
...is in your thighs!

08:54.760 --> 08:56.720
I-I see!

08:56.720 --> 09:00.390
Now all I have to do
is to wake Master Fay!

09:00.390 --> 09:03.440
Let's see if he would like
to rub my toned thighs.

09:03.770 --> 09:06.510
Don't say it like Fay is a pervert!

09:06.940 --> 09:09.950
GODS' GAME WE PLAY

09:11.910 --> 09:14.620
So there's no camera in there, huh?

09:14.620 --> 09:18.830
Bookmaker's game doesn't work
with other gods' eye lenses.

09:18.830 --> 09:22.540
So they don't allow
interference from outside, huh?

09:22.540 --> 09:27.550
I guess they set the Elements that way
because they want a 1 vs. 1 game.

09:27.990 --> 09:29.130
Are you ready?

09:30.960 --> 09:33.020
I will surely win against Bookmaker!

09:47.260 --> 09:50.430
This Elements is kind of like
a deserted casino room.

09:50.430 --> 09:53.780
Yeah. This place is so different.

09:53.780 --> 09:55.560
Where's the god?

09:55.560 --> 09:59.750
What do they want by inviting us
into such a small place?

10:00.600 --> 10:03.710
This is a multi-phase space
that reflects the heart.

10:04.670 --> 10:07.200
This place was created by your mind.

10:07.200 --> 10:09.630
This small room...

10:11.590 --> 10:14.210
...is the embodiment of your insecurities.

10:14.210 --> 10:16.570
The ceiling light is strong

10:16.570 --> 10:19.640
because you want a certain future.

10:24.730 --> 10:26.680
This casino table is magnificent, isn't it?

10:26.680 --> 10:29.980
And you seem determined
to compete with me.

10:30.700 --> 10:32.950
There are two Nel?!

10:32.950 --> 10:35.520
Ah, I'm so happy.

10:35.520 --> 10:37.510
It's been a long time
since I've seen humans.

10:38.000 --> 10:40.050
Let's play, shall we?

10:41.180 --> 10:44.370
I am Gremoire, the god of uncertainty.

10:45.590 --> 10:49.690
Mimic, Shape Shifter, Doppelganger...

10:50.440 --> 10:54.550
Humans have called me about
200 different names in the past.

10:54.550 --> 10:57.630
Bookmaker is one of them.

10:57.630 --> 11:00.640
Is "Gremoire" your favorite name?

11:00.640 --> 11:03.350
You can give me another name.

11:03.350 --> 11:05.310
Let me confirm the rules.

11:05.310 --> 11:09.010
If Nel wins in a 1 vs. 1 game against you,

11:09.010 --> 11:10.770
her one loss disappears.

11:10.770 --> 11:12.160
That's right.

11:12.160 --> 11:14.970
You can bet on one or two wins.

11:15.360 --> 11:18.490
So, do you want to bet using your wins?

11:18.490 --> 11:22.140
Yeah. I bet on Nel by using my three wins.

11:22.450 --> 11:23.330
Wha—

11:23.330 --> 11:24.800
W-What?!

11:24.800 --> 11:29.170
Wait, Master Fay!
I never heard about this!

11:29.650 --> 11:31.240
I decided on it last night.

11:31.240 --> 11:33.920
If you win, your record will be
3 wins and 0 losses at once.

11:33.920 --> 11:36.880
If Nel loses, Fay will be in big trouble!

11:36.880 --> 11:40.000
Oh, geez! Please help us, Lady Leshea!

11:40.000 --> 11:42.060
I don't mind it, though.

11:42.060 --> 11:47.020
I made a fatal mistake
by relying on you!

11:47.020 --> 11:49.810
I approved your bet.

11:49.810 --> 11:54.230
I wonder if there has ever been a human
who would bet on those wins.

11:57.620 --> 11:59.120
Three wins...

12:01.310 --> 12:02.580
Just take it easy.

12:02.980 --> 12:04.850
T-Thank you.

12:06.290 --> 12:08.180
Let's play, Gremoire!

12:08.180 --> 12:10.170
Show me your game!

12:10.590 --> 12:11.710
Poker.

12:12.150 --> 12:13.050
What?

12:13.420 --> 12:16.160
You're more familiar with
the human game, aren't you?

12:21.120 --> 12:24.430
I'm in a good mood since I haven't
had a visitor for a long time.

12:24.430 --> 12:27.140
Do not let this good fortune pass you by.

12:27.140 --> 12:31.610
And from now on,
you can't give her advice or cheer.

12:31.610 --> 12:32.590
Got it.

12:33.330 --> 12:35.840
Then, let's start the game.

12:42.530 --> 12:43.660
I'll take your challenge.

12:44.160 --> 12:46.640
I can't lose here.

12:48.560 --> 12:51.670
I cannot betray Master Fay's expectations!

12:55.290 --> 12:58.510
I saved you the trouble
of holding the cards.

12:58.510 --> 13:01.150
I can't see your cards.

13:01.150 --> 13:02.800
And I don't intend to do that.

13:04.220 --> 13:05.830
One pair of fives.

13:06.420 --> 13:09.350
If I can draw five
and make three or more cards...

13:10.180 --> 13:13.070
The game will provide
five coins for each side.

13:21.320 --> 13:22.920
Trading three coins.

13:22.920 --> 13:26.580
In other words, Nel and Gremoire
both initially had one pair.

13:26.580 --> 13:29.690
They exchange for
a three-of-a-kind hand or better.

13:30.410 --> 13:32.500
If so, Nel is at a disadvantage.

13:33.100 --> 13:36.890
Nel's card was a five,
the weakest of all one pairs.

13:36.890 --> 13:40.530
So it's unlikely that Gremoire
had a pair of fives or less.

13:43.360 --> 13:44.710
Two pair...

13:47.980 --> 13:50.890
Now, how many coins
do you want to bet?

13:50.890 --> 13:53.310
You can do it first.

13:55.580 --> 13:57.650
I bet on one coin.

13:59.440 --> 14:00.500
Raise.

14:01.200 --> 14:04.410
I bet all of my coins.

14:04.410 --> 14:06.950
All coins? You're going all in?!

14:06.950 --> 14:10.330
Is she so confident with her hand?!

14:11.140 --> 14:15.440
All you can do is accept my raise
or maybe fold your cards.

14:15.440 --> 14:18.190
Those are your two options.

14:20.920 --> 14:24.000
If she takes the call,
they bet all of each other's coins

14:24.000 --> 14:26.350
and decide this game in a single move.

14:26.350 --> 14:27.560
If she folds,

14:27.560 --> 14:29.350
she'll reject the strong raise

14:29.350 --> 14:31.440
and lose her two coins,

14:31.440 --> 14:33.210
but she has three coins left in her hand

14:33.210 --> 14:35.970
and can carry the opportunity
over to the next game.

14:36.360 --> 14:40.310
Does Gremoire really have a strong card set?

14:40.750 --> 14:43.980
Or is she just bluffing to look strong

14:43.980 --> 14:46.770
so that I will fold?

14:48.670 --> 14:50.040
Nel...

14:50.040 --> 14:53.110
If I win, my three losses will disappear,
and I can make a comeback.

14:53.580 --> 14:55.270
If only I won here...

14:57.710 --> 14:59.540
No, this is a trap!

15:00.040 --> 15:01.840
I'm not that hasty that I'd settle

15:01.840 --> 15:05.040
for less than a minute

15:05.500 --> 15:07.940
against a god like you!

15:07.940 --> 15:08.910
Fold!

15:14.350 --> 15:17.060
S-She was saved from danger.

15:17.060 --> 15:19.650
Nel's intuition is brilliant!

15:19.650 --> 15:23.520
If she had taken the call,
she would have lost all her coins.

15:23.520 --> 15:26.330
I hope that was just intuition.

15:26.790 --> 15:27.660
Huh?

15:28.440 --> 15:29.620
COINS ON HAND
Three coins left...

15:29.620 --> 15:31.580
NEL: 3 COINS - GREMOIRE: 7 COINS

15:31.900 --> 15:33.900
Let's move on to the 2nd game.

15:38.510 --> 15:41.170
No hand. This hand is weaker
than in the 1st game.

15:45.840 --> 15:47.590
How many cards
do you want to exchange?

15:47.590 --> 15:50.300
I would exchange four cards.

15:52.330 --> 15:54.300
Ace is the strongest digit.

15:54.300 --> 15:56.910
For example,
even with the weakest one pair,

15:56.910 --> 15:58.410
a pair of aces can be played

15:58.410 --> 15:59.860
depending on my opponent's hand.

15:59.860 --> 16:01.900
I exchanged one card.

16:02.790 --> 16:03.880
One card?!

16:03.880 --> 16:06.780
You mean you already have
a hand with your four cards?!

16:06.780 --> 16:09.000
FLUSH - STRAIGHT
Is she aiming for two pair,

16:09.000 --> 16:12.370
THREE-OF-A-KIND - TWO PAIR
three-of-a-kind, a flush, or a straight?

16:14.390 --> 16:17.290
Should I take a challenge to fold
with that strong bluff?

16:17.670 --> 16:21.440
But if she has a completed
hand of three cards,

16:21.440 --> 16:23.480
I doubt she'll do that.

16:24.180 --> 16:26.630
No, even if she bluffs to win,

16:27.170 --> 16:29.670
even if I lose,
I still have one coin left.

16:30.090 --> 16:32.620
I can still have a chance
to win the next hand.

16:33.930 --> 16:34.810
I bet one...

16:34.810 --> 16:36.390
Raise.

16:37.520 --> 16:41.100
I bet one coin,
and she does raise it?!

16:41.400 --> 16:43.980
In other words,
what she's trying to say is,

16:43.980 --> 16:46.700
"Bet all three of your coins."

16:47.570 --> 16:49.600
Call or fold...

16:50.100 --> 16:52.990
Now, it's time to make your choice.

16:54.840 --> 16:55.950
Fold...

16:56.260 --> 16:57.360
How unfortunate.

17:00.370 --> 17:03.460
If you had taken the call,
you would have won.

17:03.460 --> 17:05.090
No hand?!

17:05.090 --> 17:07.030
Why did you trade one card?!

17:07.030 --> 17:10.570
With your hand, you could have discarded
two cards and gone for a straight.

17:10.570 --> 17:14.550
No, you could have gone for
one pair or two pair!

17:14.550 --> 17:17.520
I don't care how strong
or weak my hand is.

17:17.520 --> 17:18.530
What?

17:18.530 --> 17:21.480
This 2nd game was a foregone conclusion.

17:21.830 --> 17:25.940
I knew you would fold if I bluffed.

17:26.610 --> 17:27.590
That's because...

17:28.270 --> 17:30.650
...you don't want to win.

17:31.240 --> 17:32.020
That's not true!

17:32.020 --> 17:34.820
No, you don't want to win.

17:34.820 --> 17:36.620
You just don't want to lose.

17:36.620 --> 17:39.880
What did you say to me
right before we began the game?

17:39.880 --> 17:40.700
What?

17:41.680 --> 17:44.000
I can't lose here.

17:44.710 --> 17:48.670
If you want to make a comeback,
you should say, "I'm going to win."

17:49.950 --> 17:51.310
I'm convinced now.

17:51.310 --> 17:53.280
You were more afraid of losing

17:53.280 --> 17:58.100
and losing your friends' winning streak
than risking to win.

17:58.100 --> 17:59.810
T-That's...

17:59.810 --> 18:04.020
Do you think you can win
without risking anything?

18:05.610 --> 18:07.960
You only have one coin left.

18:08.400 --> 18:10.940
You can't fold anymore.

18:12.530 --> 18:16.740
It's only a matter of my hand
being stronger than yours!

18:19.660 --> 18:21.540
COINS ON HAND

18:21.540 --> 18:22.950
NEL: 1 COINS - GREMOIRE: 9 COINS
One coin left...

18:23.480 --> 18:25.000
It's not over yet!

18:25.000 --> 18:27.960
Please, give her a strong hand!

18:28.440 --> 18:29.540
No hand...

18:30.960 --> 18:34.890
But if I draw 3 or 8,
I'll have a straight!

18:35.700 --> 18:37.390
I trade one card.

18:38.440 --> 18:41.940
If you trade one card,
you may at least aim for two pair,

18:41.940 --> 18:43.340
a full house...

18:43.340 --> 18:46.260
A flush, or maybe straight.

18:46.610 --> 18:48.190
But you know what they say, human?

18:48.190 --> 18:53.070
Strong hands are strong because
they don't come together so easily.

18:53.070 --> 18:55.180
I have to make it happen!

18:56.370 --> 18:58.970
If I don't draw it now, I won't...

18:58.970 --> 19:00.330
You can't draw it.

19:00.330 --> 19:04.070
The gods smile at those
who make their own miracles.

19:04.640 --> 19:06.750
You're just trapped,

19:06.750 --> 19:10.170
hoping for a last-minute miracle.

19:10.550 --> 19:13.010
God is not smiling on you.

19:13.010 --> 19:15.460
That's not true! I...

19:18.430 --> 19:19.890
No way...

19:20.850 --> 19:23.700
Not yet! It is decided by your hands!

19:23.700 --> 19:25.190
Three-of-a-kind.

19:28.730 --> 19:31.320
You should have the tactics to take the win

19:31.320 --> 19:34.270
instead of avoiding losing.

19:34.270 --> 19:36.910
You were the one who should have
challenged the bluff

19:36.910 --> 19:39.390
when trading the cards in this game.

19:40.160 --> 19:44.120
Ah, how boring.
You're way too weak.

19:44.580 --> 19:47.780
You had at least three
chances in this game.

19:48.610 --> 19:51.760
Once in a desperate attempt.
Once in tears.

19:51.760 --> 19:54.130
Once in desperation.

19:54.130 --> 19:57.590
It was you who ruined it.

20:00.430 --> 20:01.500
Nel!

20:02.220 --> 20:06.230
I had high hopes because you were
the first person in a long time to come here.

20:06.230 --> 20:10.240
You can't lose because your friends
entrusted you with their wins.

20:10.240 --> 20:12.690
But you can't take a risk.

20:12.690 --> 20:15.300
I can see that thinking.

20:15.650 --> 20:18.500
This human defeat
will not be overturned.

20:18.500 --> 20:22.120
I'll take all three of your bets.

20:27.040 --> 20:29.000
Really disappointing.

20:29.000 --> 20:31.960
I thought it would be an interesting game.

20:31.960 --> 20:33.880
You can go back, humans.

20:35.200 --> 20:36.060
Wait.

20:36.720 --> 20:38.300
The game isn't over.

20:39.620 --> 20:41.550
What are you talking about?

20:41.550 --> 20:44.150
I'm saying it was all in our calculation.

20:45.270 --> 20:46.520
Bookmaker...

20:46.520 --> 20:47.870
No, Gremoire.

20:48.440 --> 20:50.170
I win this game.

20:50.600 --> 20:51.540
What?

20:51.540 --> 20:53.940
I knew I was going to win

20:53.940 --> 20:56.050
when you decided to play this game.

20:56.430 --> 20:57.820
No matter how it turns out.

20:58.250 --> 21:01.470
That's why I told Nel to take it easy.

21:02.530 --> 21:06.060
All right, change players.
I'll play the next game.

21:06.490 --> 21:08.230
We can compare the answers later.

21:10.310 --> 21:13.060
You want to know
why I'm declaring this victory?

21:13.840 --> 21:15.710
I'll tell you why.

21:15.710 --> 21:17.460
Master Fay...

21:17.460 --> 21:19.610
You've been so supportive of me.

21:19.970 --> 21:22.760
I've decided to pay you back.

21:24.030 --> 21:26.640
You haven't played enough, have you?

21:27.020 --> 21:30.200
I'm betting on all three
of my remaining wins.

21:31.010 --> 21:33.610
If I win, I'll have Nel's loss erased.

21:35.140 --> 21:38.080
I've decided, human.

21:38.080 --> 21:39.850
Are you ready to play now?

21:39.850 --> 21:40.780
No.

21:41.120 --> 21:42.900
I've decided the game.

21:49.250 --> 21:50.430
This is...

21:55.880 --> 21:59.260
What is this world?!

22:00.090 --> 22:02.510
Welcome to the Casino of the Gods.

22:02.970 --> 22:05.400
The name of the game is Three Cheats.

22:05.400 --> 22:07.760
Let's see if you can see through

22:07.760 --> 22:09.360
my divine cheats.
